meta {
  name: Get session
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/session
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  # Get session

  `GET /api/auth/session`

  Return identity claims and the token expiry timestamp.

  ## Authentication

  Admin or Editor; inherited Bearer token.

  ## Parameters

  No path or query parameters.

  ## Request body

  No request body.

  ## Response

  HTTP **200**.

  ```json
  {
    "id": "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
    "username": "Admin",
    "email": "admin@example.com",
    "role": "Admin",
    "expiresAt": 1794700800
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  - 401: invalid/expired token or missing/unparseable exp claim.
  - 403: token role is not allowed.

  Automatic model validation can return ValidationProblemDetails; explicit controller errors use a message field. Authentication middleware errors may have no body.

  ## Notes

  expiresAt is a Unix timestamp in seconds. Uses token claims, not a fresh user database lookup. Response caching is disabled.

  Examples contain fictitious data. The assertion checks the successful scenario; a missing record or insufficient permissions can produce a different documented status.
}
